    "clinicalPearl": "Key takeaway: Positive serum cryptococcal antigen in AIDS CD4 <100 = perform LP to evaluate for cryptococcal meningitis (India ink, CSF cryptococcal antigen, opening pressure). If CNS disease: lipo-amphotericin B + flucytosine x 2 wk → fluconazole 8 wk → chronic suppression + therapeutic LPs. Delay ART 2-4 wk to reduce IRIS. If CSF negative: fluconazole for cryptococcal antigenemia.",
